-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ט/1 — תשלום תוספת השכר בגין השעה הפרטנית בשיעור 4.5% בחודשי הקיץ (25.9.2008)
-- On the Treasury's letter of 10.9.2008, the 4.5% individual-hour
-- supplement is paid after all for July–August 2008, pro-rated by the part
-- of the school year's employment in which the hour was done; it is not paid
-- from 1.9.2008, and the State indemnifies the owning bodies.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשלום תוספת השעה הפרטנית בחודשי הקיץ`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (25.9.2008), and the recital: further to circular תשס"ח/7 of 16.7.2008, it has now been decided, on the deputy wage commissioner's letter of 10.9.2008, to pay the supplement for July–August 2008; no rule beyond what §§1–4 set.

@desc A teaching employee of an owning body, as far as the summer supplement asks about them.
DECLARE `summer case` HAS
    `did the individual hour under the 24.1.2008 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months employed in the school year`        IS A NUMBER  @desc months employed in the 2007-08 school year (September 2007 to August 2008), 12 for the whole year
    `months in which the hour was done`         IS A NUMBER  @desc months of that employment in which the employee did the individual hour (the hour ran from January 2008)
    `the month's supplement base`               IS A NUMBER  @desc the salary components the 4.5% is computed on under the 24.1.2008 agreement, for one month, already by the position fraction; an input

DECLARE `summer action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the individual-hour supplement for July-August 2008` HAS `summer amount` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the individual-hour supplement for a month from 1.9.2008`
    `indemnify the owning body for the payments` HAS `indemnity amount` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `summer party` IS ONE OF
    `the owning body`
    `the State`

§§ `1`

-- §1: the owning body is to pay the individual-hour supplement of 4.5% for
-- July–August 2008 to the teaching employees it employs who did the
-- individual hour under the collective agreement of 24.1.2008. The amount
-- is §2's.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN c IS A `summer case`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `summer party` `summer action`
DECIDE `the owning body pays the supplement for July-August 2008` c IS
    IF c's `did the individual hour under the 24.1.2008 agreement`
    THEN PARTY `the owning body`
         MUST  `pay the individual-hour supplement for July-August 2008` x
               PROVIDED x AT LEAST `the summer supplement` c
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:art_1
`the individual-hour supplement rate` MEANS 4.5%

§§ `2`

-- §2: the supplement for these months is multiplied by the share of the
-- school year's employment in which the hour was done. The reading adopted
-- (F-2008-09_tashsat_01-a): months in which the hour was actually done over
-- all the months employed in the school year.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN c IS A `summer case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement for one summer month` c IS
    IF c's `did the individual hour under the 24.1.2008 agreement`
    THEN `the individual-hour supplement rate` TIMES c's `the month's supplement base`
         TIMES `the share of the year the hour was done` c
    ELSE 0

GIVEN c IS A `summer case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the year the hour was done` c IS
    IF c's `months employed in the school year` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN min 1 (c's `months in which the hour was done` DIVIDED BY c's `months employed in the school year`)
    ELSE 0

@export The 4.5% individual-hour supplement owed for July and August 2008 together under circular 2008-09/1
GIVEN c IS A `summer case` @desc the teaching employee's 2007-08 year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the summer supplement` c IS
    2 TIMES `the supplement for one summer month` c

§§ `3`

-- §3: the agreement on the individual hour has expired, and the 4.5%
-- supplement is not paid to teaching employees of the owning bodies from
-- 1.9.2008. No time limit: the prohibition stands.
@ref akn:art_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC `summer party` `summer action`
DECIDE `no individual-hour supplement from 1.9.2008` IS
    PARTY `the owning body`
    SHANT `pay the individual-hour supplement for a month from 1.9.2008`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the owning body` BECAUSE "section 3: the individual-hour agreement has expired; the 4.5% supplement is not paid from 1.9.2008"

-- The same as a test on a month of 2008: September is 9.
GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement is payable for 2008 month` month IF
    month AT MOST 8

§§ `4`

-- §4: the State indemnifies the owning bodies for "these payments" — §1's.
-- No date is printed.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN `amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc what the owning body paid under section 1
GIVETH A DEONTIC `summer party` `summer action`
DECIDE `the State indemnifies the owning body` `amount paid` IS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `indemnify the owning body for the payments` y
          PROVIDED y AT LEAST `amount paid`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, New Year greeting and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_01-a: a full-year teacher who did the hour every month
-- it ran (January–June 2008) has 6 of 12 months on the reading adopted, 6
-- of 10 if the school year is its teaching months, and 8 of 12 if July–August
-- count as months in which the hour was done.
`a full-year teacher who did the hour from January` MEANS
    `summer case` WITH
        `did the individual hour under the 24.1.2008 agreement` IS TRUE
        `months employed in the school year`        IS 12
        `months in which the hour was done`         IS 6
        `the month's supplement base`               IS 10000

`§2's share reads three ways` MEANS
        `the share of the year the hour was done` `a full-year teacher who did the hour from January` EQUALS 1/2
    AND NOT (6 DIVIDED BY 10 EQUALS 1/2)
    AND NOT (8 DIVIDED BY 12 EQUALS 1/2)
#ASSERT `§2's share reads three ways`

-- Example: a base of 10,000 is a placeholder. 4.5% × 10,000 × 1/2 = 225 a
-- month, 450 for July–August.
#ASSERT `the summer supplement` `a full-year teacher who did the hour from January` EQUALS 450
#ASSERT NOT `the supplement is payable for 2008 month` 9

#TRACE `the owning body pays the supplement for July-August 2008` `a full-year teacher who did the hour from January` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owning body` DOES `pay the individual-hour supplement for July-August 2008` 450 AT 1
#TRACE `the State indemnifies the owning body` 450 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State` DOES `indemnify the owning body for the payments` 450 AT 2
#TRACE `no individual-hour supplement from 1.9.2008` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owning body` DOES `pay the individual-hour supplement for a month from 1.9.2008` AT 1
